    <item>
      <title>C&#43;&#43; Variant From Scratch</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/posts/variant/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 26 Jul 2025 23:34:30 +0200</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/posts/variant/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;c-variant-from-scratch&#34;&gt;C++ Variant From Scratch&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE&lt;/strong&gt;: As of 26. july, this post is still incomplete. I&amp;rsquo;m sure I&amp;rsquo;ll get&#xA;around to it eventually. Don&amp;rsquo;t expect any kind of mind-blowing writing prowess to shine through just yet.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;For quite some time now, I&amp;rsquo;ve been wanting to do a full-scale implementation&#xA;of &lt;code&gt;std::variant&lt;/code&gt; from scratch. Why would you want to put yourself through&#xA;the torment, you ask? Here&amp;rsquo;s what I say:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Your understanding of the STL deepens.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Your template metaprogramming chops get their much needed exercise.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;You get your chance to make your sacrifice to the ever-benevolent standards library devs.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;By the end of this exercise you&amp;rsquo;re likely going to fall into one of two categories (insert there are 10 kinds of people joke here):&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Hello</title>
